      "title": "Incident Escalation Service Recovery Runbook — 2. Escalation Targets",
      "text": "Every incident may optionally have an `escalationTarget` that routes ownership: | Target | Role | When to use | | ------------------ | ----------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- | | `ops_supervisor` | Ops shift supervisor | Standard operational incidents | | `dispatch_manager` | Dispatch operations manager | Dispatch-related exceptions and failures | | `safety_officer` | Safety and compliance officer | Safety, injury, and property damage incidents | | `roc_duty` | ROC duty officer | Critical incidents requiring immediate command coordination | Escalation targets are set during incident creation or updated via the incident edit form. Each change is recorded in the incident timeline with actor and timestamp.",
