      "snippetId": "5c95800349fa6385",
      "title": "Incident Escalation Service Recovery Runbook — 4. Dispatch Exception to Incident Handoff",
      "text": "When a dispatch order enters `exception_hold` status, operators can create a formal incident from the dispatch console. The handoff: 1. Operator clicks \"Escalate to incident\" on the exception-hold order card in the dispatch workflow page. 2. The system pre-fills the incident with: - Order ID and exception reason code from the dispatch exception - Operational category - The exception note as the description 3. The `sourceDispatchExceptionOrderId` field preserves the link back to the original dispatch order, ensuring the full trace chain is not broken. 4. A `dispatch_exception_handoff` timeline entry is created automatically.",
      "normalizedText": "incident escalation service recovery runbook — 4. dispatch exception to incident handoff when a dispatch order enters `exception_hold` status, operators can create a formal incident from the dispatch console. the handoff: 1. operator clicks \"escalate to incident\" on the exception-hold order card in the dispatch workflow page. 2. the system pre-fills the incident with: - order id and exception reason code from the dispatch exception - operational category - the exception note as the description 3. the `sourcedispatchexceptionorderid` field preserves the link back to the original dispatch order, ensuring the full trace chain is not broken. 4. a `dispatch_exception_handoff` timeline entry is created automatically.",
